course: dictionary
lesson: 10969
title: The wanderer
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A wanderer is a person or animal that travels from place to place with no fixed home or clear plan. Use the context to check. «Sea turtles are the great wanderers» is followed by a baby crawling to the sea and swimming thousands of kilometres, so a wanderer must travel very far.
explain: Wanderer can also mean someone who likes to roam and explore. In stories, a wanderer is often a traveller or a lonely figure on the road, which gives a feeling of freedom or loneliness. Look for clues like «a lonely wanderer» to see which feeling the author wants.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «A planet looks like a bright star, but over weeks it slowly wanders among the constellations» still makes sense if wanders means moves slowly from place to place. The meaning fits, so you can trust it.
fact: A wanderer is a person or animal that travels from place to place with no fixed home or clear plan.
fact: «A lonely wanderer» is a common phrase in stories, often about a traveller on the road.
fact: «The wanderer returns» means someone who travelled away has come back home.
fact: The word planet comes from a Greek word meaning wanderer, because planets move across the night sky against the stars.
fact: Wanderer can also mean someone who likes to roam and explore.
exercise: «Sea turtles are the great wanderers.» What does wanderers mean here? | *Animals that travel very far with no fixed home | Animals that stay in one nest all their lives | Fish that live in rivers | Birds that sing at night
exercise: Why does the word planet come from a Greek word meaning wanderer? | *Planets move across the night sky against the stars | Planets only appear in the morning | Planets are very small and hard to see | Planets are always cold and dark
exercise: In «swims thousands of kilometres for years», what does thousands of kilometres show? | *A very long journey | Slow sleeping under the sand | A bright light in the sky | A short walk to the shops
test: Which phrase suggests a wanderer might feel alone? | *A lonely wanderer | A happy family party | A busy market full of people | Loud music in the street
test: The word planet comes from which language? | Scots | *Greek | Latin | French
exam: Which of these best describes a wanderer? | Someone who sits still all day in one chair | A large house with many rooms | *Someone who travels from place to place with no fixed home | A bright star that never moves
